<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="039" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Deploy Phase 2 to dev; FR-13 restart check; routing-eval run B</title>
    <phase>2 Long-running work, AI, widgets, task writes</phase>
    <gate>BLOCKED until the owner gives a go for the exact SHA in uac-r2's session; the App Service restart needs a separate owner go</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deployment task with live verification</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Deployment through the bff-deploy skill plus scripted probes; judgment points are escalation triggers</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>J</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Live deployment and restart of the shared dev BFF; runs alone</parallel-reason>
    <deps>029, 030, 031, 032, 033, 034, 035, 036</deps>
    <tags>deploy, azure, app-service, bff-api</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Deploy the merged Phase 2 BFF (run, analysis, matter summary, finance, briefing, task writes and two widgets) to dev through uac-r2's session after the owner's go for the exact SHA; verify each new tool and both widgets as the test user; with a separate owner go, restart the dev App Service and prove a run started before the restart is still readable (FR-13); prepare routing-eval run B (≈18 tools).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in Azure App Service deployment and MCP probing.</role>
  <goal>The approved SHA runs on dev; start-then-status round-trips for runs and the matter summary; the briefing and search widgets render in Chat; a pre-restart run's status reads back from Dataverse after the restart over REST and MCP; notes/routing-eval-B.md is ready for the owner.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-05 and FR-13 acceptance (start/status on dev; survives a BFF restart), FR-10 (≤ 3 s cached), FR-16, FR-17 (run B ≈ 15 tools; planning count ≈18 model-visible). Deploy shape: task 019/029. r1 eval method: projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/routing-eval.md.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="output">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/deploy-dev-039.md</file>
      <file role="output">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/routing-eval-B.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/tasks/029-deploy-phase1-dev.poml</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="029" status="pending">Phase 1 on dev</dependency>
      <dependency task="036" status="pending">Last Phase 2 task merged</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Deploy only after the owner's explicit go for the exact SHA, in uac-r2's session, with the bff-deploy skill; never raw az webapp deploy --clean; dev only; no App Service setting change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The restart (az webapp restart on the dev BFF only) happens only after a separate explicit owner go recorded in the note; if not given, record FR-13's live check as pending and finish the rest.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Write probes (start a run, create/complete a task, start an analysis) use test data on test matters as the test user, are recorded, and are cleaned up or marked as test data; never on real matters.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Record the published size (at or under 60 MB; 55 MB or more triggers architecture review) in the deploy note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Never log or store the test user's token (NFR-05). Run context-handoff after the deploy.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/bff-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/routing-eval.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Record the owner's go for SHA {sha} in notes/deploy-dev-039.md; if missing, stop. Run /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="2">Deploy with the bff-deploy skill in uac-r2's session; record the rollback SHA and publish size.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify each Phase 2 tool once as the test user; start a playbook run and poll it to completion; call spaarke_get_matter_summary twice (start, then cached ≤ 3 s); render the briefing and search widgets in Copilot Chat.</step>
    <step order="4">With the owner's restart go: start a run, restart the dev App Service, read the run over GET /api/ai/playbooks/runs/{runId} and spaarke_get_playbook_run; record both.</step>
    <step order="5">Write notes/routing-eval-B.md; hand it to the owner. Run context-handoff.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the owner has not given a go for this exact SHA, STOP.</trigger>
    <trigger>If /healthz or any tool fails after deploy, roll back to the recorded SHA and escalate.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the run is not readable after the restart, record it as an FR-13 defect against 005 and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pwsh">scripts/Deploy-BffApi.ps1 via the bff-deploy skill</tool>
    <tool name="az">az webapp restart (dev BFF, after the owner's restart go)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="deploy">dev BFF at the approved SHA</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/deploy-dev-039.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/routing-eval-B.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/deploy-dev-039.md records the owner's go with the exact SHA, deployed and rollback SHAs, the publish size and each probe's outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Start-then-status round-trips on dev for spaarke_run_playbook and spaarke_get_matter_summary; the cached matter summary returns in ≤ 3 s.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">After the owner-approved restart, a pre-restart run's status is returned by both REST and spaarke_get_playbook_run (or the note records the restart go as not given).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Briefing and search widgets render in Copilot Chat.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: without the recorded go, no deploy and no restart happened.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-05, FR-10, FR-13, FR-16, FR-17.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
